      "message": "Hi TJ, \n\nYou are right, the fallback to looking up the page cache folio, if no ptes, needs to use a 16KB unit pgoff.\n\nThe loop steps through 4KB increments but `linear_page_index()` maps each address to a pagecache index in 16KB units, so the four 4KB subpages within one 16KB page all resolve to the same index and report the same residency.\n\nIOW the `PAGE_SHIFT` in linear_page_index() (and functions defined in headers) is always the kernel `PAGE_SHIFT` the dynamic page-shift (redefinition) is only every applied to .c files (translation units).",
